1
00:05:28,235 --> 00:05:34,235
Wrongfully accused. Unjustly imprisoned. Now he's fighting back.

2
00:10:56,470 --> 00:11:02,470
Undisputed II: Last Man Standing is a action, crime,
thriller film directed by Isaac Florentine.

3
00:16:24,705 --> 00:16:30,705
Heavyweight Champ George "Iceman" Chambers is sent to a
Russian jail on trumped-up drug charges.

4
00:21:52,941 --> 00:21:58,941
In order to win his freedom he must fight against the jailhouse
fighting champ Uri Boyka in a battle to the death.

5
00:27:21,176 --> 00:27:27,176
This time he is not fighting for a title, he is fighting for his life!

6
00:32:49,411 --> 00:32:55,411
George Chambers, played by Michael Jai White.

7
00:38:17,647 --> 00:38:23,647
Yuri Boyka, played by Scott Adkins.

8
00:43:45,882 --> 00:43:51,882
Steven Parker, played by Ben Cross.

9
00:49:14,117 --> 00:49:20,117
Crot, played by Eli Danker.

10
00:54:42,352 --> 00:54:48,352
Gaga, played by Mark Ivanir.

11
01:00:10,588 --> 01:00:16,588
Phil, played by Ken Lerner.

12
01:05:38,823 --> 01:05:44,823
Undisputed II: Last Man Standing is a 2006 American direct-to-video martial arts action film directed by
Isaac Florentine and starring Michael Jai White, Scott Adkins, Eli Danker and Ben Cross.

13
01:11:07,058 --> 01:11:13,058
It is the sequel to the boxing movie Undisputed (2002), and the
second installment in the Undisputed franchise.

14
01:16:35,294 --> 01:16:41,294
White portrays ex-boxer George "Iceman" Chambers, a role
originally played by Ving Rhames in the first film.

15
01:22:03,529 --> 01:22:09,529
It was followed by two sequels: Undisputed III: Redemption (2010) and Boyka: Undisputed (2017),
which continues the story of Russian prison fighter Yuri Boyka, played by Adkins.

16
01:27:31,764 --> 01:27:37,764
The tone is emotional and intense.
